s correct decisions quickly, 100% reliable, creates positive crew atmosphere, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. No stress handling evidence.\n\nWe can argue that decision quality is critical, but we have no evidence for B, but also no evidence for C's stress handling. However, B's stress handling is documented, which is essential for long-haul. Also B's conscientiousness suggests responsibility, even though not explicit. The lack of decision quality evidence could be addressed with further assessment. Meanwhile C's communication issues and lack of adaptability may be more problematic for crew cooperation. Also C's egocentric attitude may affect crew. So we can keep B.\n\nThus we will keep vote for Candidate B, stating that despite missing decision quality evidence, B's proven stress resilience and conscientiousness outweigh C's communication and adaptability concerns, and that we can address decision quality through training. Also note that B's nasty remarks are not proven to impact safety.\n\nWe must reference Anna's point and respond.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B."}
